{title: All Things Bright and Beautiful}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]All things [F]bright and [C]beauti[C]ful, all [Dm]creatures [G]great and [C]small[**]
[C]All things [F]wise and [C]wonder[C]ful, The [Dm]Lord God [G]made them [C]all[**].
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Each [C]little [C]flower that [F]opens, each [G]little [G]bird that [C]sings
He [C]made their [Am]glowing [Dm]col[G]ors, He [C]made their [G]tiny [C]wings.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
The [C]purple-[C]headed [F]mountain, The [G]river [G]running [C]by
The [C]sun[Am]set and the [Dm]mor[G]ning, that [C]brightens [G]up the [C]sky.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 3}
The [C]cold wind [C]in the [F]winter, The [G]pleasant [G]summer [C]sun
The [C]ripe fruits [Am]in the [Dm]gar[G]den, He [C]made them, [G]every [C]one.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 4}
He g[C]ave us [C]eyes to [F]see them, and [G]lips that [G]we might [C]tell
How [C]great is [Am]God Al[Dm]migh[G]ty, who has [C]made all [G]things [C]well.
{end_of_verse}
